/-ai
At stage 4 to the n, the found flag of the X-fold is 1.

The right-to-left direction of the found-flag equivalence is applied to the existence of a non-junk half-step atom strictly below 4 to the n.
ai-/
module

public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812c
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.ComputabilityInEffectivelyGivenDomains.Definition71
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.ComputabilityInEffectivelyGivenDomains.Definition72
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.ComputabilityInEffectivelyGivenDomains.Exercise718
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.IsComputableSplit
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.IsComputableDiff
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.IsComputableUnion
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.stateIdx0_packState2
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.stateIdx1_packState2
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.stateJunk_packState2
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.stateRemC_packStateC
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.stateInnerC_packStateC
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.XFold
public import DomainTheory.NeighbourhoodSystems.RetractsOfTheUniversalDomain.Exercise812d.XFold_found_iff
